          %h2#the_spectral_sequence The spectral sequence
          %p We would like to understand the following theorem.
          %p
            %strong Theorem.
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ( X, \mathbf{O})
            be a derived Deligne-Mumford stack. Then there is a spectral sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi t
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo −
                      %mi s
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^s (X ; \pi_t \mathbf{O}) \Rightarrow \pi_{t-s} \Gamma (X , \mathbf{O}).
          %h3#recalling_what_is_what Recalling what is what
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be an
            = succeed "-topos," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is ‘’sheaves of spaces on an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed ".\u2019\u2018" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{O}
            is a functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi O
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{O} : \{ E_\infty \}^{op} \to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            formally assigns
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \mapsto (U \mapsto \mathrm{Hom} (A , \mathbf{O} (U))).
          %p
            Via DAG V 2.2.1 we can make sense of global sections and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma (X , \mathbf{O})
            is an
            = succeed "-ring." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          %p
            Given an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            we can form the subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %em truncated objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi n
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{\le n} C
            which consists of all objects such that all mapping spaces have trivial homotopy groups above level
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{\le n} : C \to C
            defines a functor which serves the role of the Postnikov decomposition.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be an
            = succeed "-topos," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Disc
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 0
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Disc} \; X : = \tau_{\le 0} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Disc
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n : X_* \to N (\mathrm{Disc} \; X)
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 0
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Map
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \mapsto \tau_{\le 0} \mathrm{Map} (S^n , Y) = \pi_n (Y) .
          %p
            %strong Facts.
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Disc
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathrm{Disc} \; X
                an abelian group object there exists
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A,n) \in X
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Map
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n (X, A) := \pi_0 \mathrm{Map} (1_X , K(A,n))
              %p
                corresponds to sections of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A,n)
                along the identity of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is an ordinary site,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n (X, A)
                corresponds to ordinary sheaf cohomology (HTT 7.2.2.17).
          %h3#the_nonderived_descent_ss The non-derived descent ss
          %p
            Let us define a mapping space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Tot
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Tot} \; X = \mathrm{hom}^\Delta (\Delta , X)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Tot
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi lim
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi …
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Tot
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Tot
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi …
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Tot
                    %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Tot} \; X = \lim ( \dots \to \mathrm{Tot}^n \; X \to \mathrm{Tot}^{n-1} \; X \to \dots \to \mathrm{Tot}^0 \to * ) ,
          %p
            where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Tot
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Tot
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} cosk
                      %mi n
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Tot}^n \; X = \mathrm{Tot} (\mathrm{cosk}_n X )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Tot
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Tot
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_n \to \mathrm{Tot}^n \; X \to \mathrm{Tot}^{n-1} \; X
          %p and it is a fact that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi s
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_s \simeq \Omega^s ( \prod_{|I|=s+1} \mathbf{O} (U_I )),
          %p
            for the fibered product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_I
            corresponding to the cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ U_i \to N\}
            of an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            of the etale site of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{1,1}
          %p
            Applying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_*
            to the cofiber sequence we obtain an exact couple and hence a spectral sequence with
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ,
                      %mi s
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo −
                      %mi s
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi s
                  %mo ⇒
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo −
                      %mi s
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Tot
                    %mi n
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo −
                      %mi s
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Tot
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo −
                      %mi s
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^1_{t,s} = \pi_{t-s} F_s \Rightarrow \lim_n \pi_{t-s} \mathrm{Tot}^n X  = \pi_{t-s} \mathrm{Tot} X = \pi_{t-s} \mathbf{O} (N).
          %p
            Note that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo −
                      %mi s
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{t-s} F_s
            is the Čech complex of the cover, so the
            = succeed "-page" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^2
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi lim
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim^1 =0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ,
                      %mi s
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi t
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^2_{t,s} \Rightarrow H^s (N, \pi_t \mathbf{O}) .
          %h2#stacks_and_hopf_algebroids Stacks and Hopf Algebroids
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a (non-derived) Deligne-Mumford stack on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Aff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Aff}
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} \; A \to X
            be a faithfully flat cover, then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} \; A \times_X \mathrm{Spec} \; A = \mathrm{Spec} \; \Gamma,
          %p
            for some commutative ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Aff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Aff}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebroid"} commutative Hopf algebroid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, \Gamma)
          %p
            Now let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\Gamma)
            be a commutative Hopf algebroid, then the collection of principal bundles form a stack
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{A,\Gamma}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} \; \Gamma
            equivariant map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to \mathrm{Spec} \; A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                        %mi A
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \times_{\mathrm{Spec} A} \mathrm{Spec} \; \Gamma \to P
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi DM
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Stacks
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi Hopf
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Algebroids
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi bibundles
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{DM \; Stacks\} \simeq \{Hopf \; Algebroids, \; bibundles\} .
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi DM
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi stacks
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi equipped
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi with
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi cover
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi Hopf
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi algebroids
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi functors
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi of
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi groupoids
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{DM \; stacks \; equipped \; with \; cover\} \simeq \{Hopf \; algebroids, \; functors \; of \; groupoids\}.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a scheme then a sheaf of abelian groups is a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Aff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ab
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{I} : \mathrm{Aff}/X^{op} \to \mathrm{Ab} .
          %p
            The structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi O
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{O}_X
            is defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi O
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{O}_X ( \mathrm{Spec} \; A \to X) = A .
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{I}
            be a sheaf of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi O
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{O}_X
            modules.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{I}
            is quasi-coherent if for any map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} \; B \to \mathrm{Spec} \; A
            and maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: \mathrm{Spec} \; A \to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: \mathrm{Spec} \; B \to X
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                  %mi ℑ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℑ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \otimes_{A} \mathfrak{I} (f) \simeq \mathfrak{I} (g) .
          %p
            We have an equivalence of categories
            = succeed "-mod" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} QCSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{QCSh}/\mathrm{Spec} \; A \simeq A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{I} \mapsto \mathfrak{I} (1_A)
          %p
            Now consider the stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{A,\Gamma}
            from above. One can show that quasi-coherent sheaves over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{A, \Gamma}
            is nothing but a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\Gamma)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comodule"} comodule
            = succeed "-module," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi Γ
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 1
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \to \Gamma \otimes^{d_1}_{A} M
          %p
            where the right hand side is an
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0
          %h2#cohomology_of_sheaves Cohomology of Sheaves
          %p
            Recall that sheaf cohomology is obtained by deriving the global sections functor. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noetherian+scheme"} noetherian
            scheme/stack then we restrict to deriving
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} QCSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ab
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma (-) : \mathrm{QCSh}/X \to \mathrm{Ab} .
          %p
            Suppose further that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \mathrm{Spec} \; A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            lands in
            = succeed "-modules," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-mod," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} QCSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{QCSh}/\mathrm{Spec} \; A \simeq A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            is exact and all higher cohomology groups vanish.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{I}_N
            be a quasi-coherent sheaf on a DM stack
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{A,\Gamma}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{I}_N
            induce global sections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in N
            such that the two pullbacks to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            correspond to each other
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 0
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi Γ
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 1
                  %mi N
                  %mo ;
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi n
                  %mo ↦
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi n
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \otimes_A^{d_0} N \to \Gamma \otimes_A^{d_1} N; \; 1 \otimes n \mapsto 1 \otimes n .
          %p
            That is the coaction map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ↦
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \mapsto 1 \otimes n
            is well defined and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                  %mo ;
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n: A \to N; \; 1 \mapsto n
            is a map of comodules. This allows us to interpret global sections as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Comod
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo −
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} mod
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Hom}_{A,\Gamma} (A, -) : \mathrm{Comod}_{A,\Gamma} \to A-\mathrm{mod} ,
          %p so a section is a map from the trivial sheaf to the given sheaf. It follows that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ext
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n ( M_{A,\Gamma} , \mathfrak{I}_N ) = \mathrm{Ext}^n_{A,\Gamma} (A,N) .
          %p
            To simplify notation we write the above as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ;
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n (A, \Gamma ; N)
            and if the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is suppressed it is assumed that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=A
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                cobar complex
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/cobar+complex"} ?
          %h3#change_of_rings Change of Rings
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\Gamma)
            be a commutative Hopf algebroid and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to B
            a ring homomorphism. Define
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %mi B
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 0
                  %mi Γ
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 1
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_B = B \otimes_A^{d_0} \Gamma \otimes_A^{d_1} B ,
          %p
            so we have a map of Hopf algebroids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* : (A, \Gamma) \to (B, \Gamma_B)
            and of stacks
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* : M_{B,\Gamma_B} \to M_{A,\Gamma} .
          %p
            %strong Theorem.
            If there exists a ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            and a homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \otimes_A B \to R
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to \Gamma \otimes_A B \to R
          %p
            is faithfully flat, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            is an equivalence of stacks.
          %h3#the_weierstrass_stack The Weierstrass Stack
          %p
            Given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/S
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann-Roch+theorem"} Riemann–Roch
            gives us (locally on
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \Gamma (C, \mathbf{O} (2e)) , \; y \in \Gamma (C, \mathbf{O} (3e))
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 3
                  %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 5
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^3-y^2 \in \Gamma (C, \mathbf{O}(5e))
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %munder
                      %mi a
                      %mo ̲
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \simeq C_{\underline{a}} \subset \mathbb{P}^2
            is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mi xy
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 3
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 4
                  %mi X
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 6
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y^2 + a_1 xy + a_3 y = x^3 +a_2 x^2 +a_4 X + a_6
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi O
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_i \in \mathbf{O}_S
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e = [0: 1:0]
          %p
            Two Weierstrass curves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %munder
                      %mi a
                      %mo ̲
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C_\underline{a} , e)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mi a
                        %mo ̲
                      %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C_{\underline{a}'},e)
            are isomorphic if and only if they are related by a coordinate change of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                  %mi X
                  %mo +
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 3
                  %mi y
                  %mo +
                  %mi s
                  %msup
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,Y) \mapsto (\lambda^{-2} X + r, \lambda^{-3} y + s \lambda^{-2} x +t ) .
          %p
            For instance, this means that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1'= \lambda (a_1 +2s)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, \Gamma)
            by defining
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 6
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ±
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathbb{Z} [a_1 , \dots , a_4 , a_6 ] , \; \Gamma = A [r,s,t, \lambda^\pm ] .
          %p
            Further, define the stacks
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi Weir
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{Weir} = M_{A, \Gamma}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi ell
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{ell} = M_{A[\Delta^{-1}] , \Gamma[\Delta^{-1}]}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi ell
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi ell
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi Weir
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{ell} \subset \overline{M_{ell}} \subset M_{Weir} .
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_{C/S} = \pi_* \Omega^1_{C/S}
            (which is locally free) and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi O
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{2n} \mathbf{O} = \omega^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a Weierstrass curve, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is free with generator of degree 2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mi dx
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi y
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 3
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta = \frac{dx}{2y + a_1 x +a_3} .
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega^*
            correspond to the graded comodule
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi η
                    %mo ±
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi η
                    %mo ±
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo *
                  %mo ;
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi η
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi η
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_* = A [ \eta^\pm ] \to \Gamma [\eta^\pm ] = \Gamma_* ; \; \eta \mapsto \lambda^{-1} \eta .
          %p It is classical that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 6
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mn 12
                    %mn 3
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo −
                  %msubsup
                    %mi c
                    %mn 4
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %msubsup
                    %mi c
                    %mn 6
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{0,*} (A, \Gamma ; A_*) = \mathbb{Z} [c_4 , c_6 , \Delta]/ (12^3 \Delta -c_4^3 +c_6^2 )
          %p that is the ring of modular forms. So we get a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi modular
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi forms
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_* tmf \to \{modular \; forms \}
          %p as the edge homomorphism of our spectral sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo −
                      %mi s
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{s,t} (A,\Gamma ; A_*) \simeq H^{s,t} (A_* , \Gamma_*) \Rightarrow \pi_{t-s} tmf .
          %p
            It should be noted that we have a comparison map with the Adams-Novikov spectral sequence for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
          %h2#local_coefficients
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            \-local Coefficients
          %h3#with_6_inverted With 6 inverted
          %p Note that if 2 is invertible than we can complete the square in the Weierstrass equation to obtain
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi y
                      %mo ¯
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 4
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 4
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 4
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 6
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{y}^2 = x^3 + 1/4 b_2 x^2 + 1/2 b_4 x + 1/4 b_6
          %p
            and the only automorphisms of the curve are
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto x+r
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi y
                      %mo ¯
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo ¯
                    %mn 3
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 48
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 4
                  %mover
                    %mi x
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 864
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 6
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{y}^2 = \overline{x}^3 -1/48 c_4 \overline{x} -1/864 c_6
          %p
            and this curve is rigid. Define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 6
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C= \mathbb{Z} [c_4 , c_6 ]
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_C = C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 6
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 6
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 6
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 6
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{s,*} (A_* , \Gamma_* ) [1/6] \simeq H^{s,*} (C,C) [1/6] = \mathbb{Z} [1/6 , c_4 , c_6 ]
          %p
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s=0
            and 0 otherwise.
          %h3#localized_at_3 Localized at 3
          %p
            It is true that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{s,t} (A_* , \Gamma_* ) = H^{s,t} (B, \Gamma_B)
            where
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 6
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ;
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mn 12
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = \mathbb{Z}_{(3)} [ b_2 , b_4, b_6 ] \to \Gamma_B = B[r] ; \; b_2 \mapsto b_2 + 12r
          %p
            and the degree of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            is 4. We have the class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha = [r] \in H^{1,4}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi r
                    %mo +
                    %mi r
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 12
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta = [ -1/2 (r^2 \otimes r + r \otimes r^2)] \in H^{2,12}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = (3 , b_2 , b_4 )
            and consider the Hopf algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B/I , \Gamma_B /I)
            which by change of rings theorem is equivalent to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi F
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi F
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{F}_3 , \mathbf{F}_3 [r]/(r^3))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            gives:
          %p
            %strong Theorem.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 6
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{*,*} (B, \Gamma_B) = \mathbb{Z} [c_4 , c_6 , \Delta , \alpha, \beta ]
            subject to the following relations
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 12
                        %mn 3
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo −
                      %msubsup
                        %mi c
                        %mn 4
                        %mn 3
                      %mo +
                      %msubsup
                        %mi c
                        %mn 6
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi α
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 3
                      %mi α
                      %mo =
                      %mn 3
                      %mi β
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ;
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 12^3 \Delta -c_4^3 +c_6^2 = \alpha^2 = 3\alpha = 3 \beta =0;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 4
                      %mi α
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 6
                      %mi α
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 4
                      %mi β
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 6
                      %mi β
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_4 \alpha = c_6 \alpha = c_4 \beta = c_6 \beta = 0.
          %p By using the comparison map with the Adams-Novikov spectral sequence one can prove the following theorem.
          %p
            %strong Theorem.
            The edge homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi tmf
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi Modular
                  %mi Forms
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_* tmf_{(3)} \to \{Modular Forms\}_{(3)}
            has
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Cokernel given by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 3
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/3\mathbb{Z} [\Delta^n]
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \ge 0
                and not divisble by 3;
            %li
              %p
                Kernel consisting a copy of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 3
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/3\mathbb{Z}
                in degrees 3,10,13,20,27,30,37,40 modulo 72. This is the 3-torsion in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mo *
                        %mi tmf
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_* tmf
          %p For more see
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tilman+Bauer"}> Tilman Bauer
            ,
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Computation of the homotopy of the spectrum tmf
            = succeed ".," do
              %em Geom. Topol. Monogr
